221l</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Perreira M, Jiang JK, Klutz AM, Gao Z-G, Shainberg A, Lu C, Thomas CJ, Jacobson KA (2005) &#x0201c;Reversine&#x0201d; and its 2-substituted adenine derivatives as potent and selective A3 adenosine receptor antagonists. J Med Chem 48:4910&#x02013;4918 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16033270</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR24"><label>24.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jacobson</surname><given-names>KA</given-names></name><name><surname>Ohno</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Duong</surname><given-names>HT</given-names></name><name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>SK</given-names></name><name><surname>Tchilibon</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Cesnek</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Holy</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Gao</surname><given-names>Z-G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A neoceptor approach to unraveling microscopic interactions between the human A<sub>2A</sub> adenosine receptor and its agonists</article-title><source>Chem Biol</source><year>2005</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>237</fpage><lpage>247</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.chembiol.2004.12.010</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Jacobson KA, Ohno M, Duong HT, Kim SK, Tchilibon S, Cesnek M, Holy A, Gao Z-G (2005) A neoceptor approach to unraveling microscopic interactions between the human A2A adenosine receptor and its agonists. Chem Biol 12:237&#x02013;247 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15734651</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR25"><label>25.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Niebauer</surname><given-names>RT</given-names></name><name><surname>Gao</surname><given-names>Z-G</given-names></name><name><surname>Li</surname><given-names>B</given-na